<title>JAPAN: Nippon Mining lowers indium price by 4,000 yen.</title>
<headline>Nippon Mining lowers indium price by 4,000 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Mining and Metals Co said on Tuesday that it had lowered its selling price for indium ingot by 4,000 yen to 26,000 yen per kg for large orders and 31,000 yen per kg for small orders for 99.99 percent pure metal.</p>
<p>The price is effective from October 9 shipments.</p>
<p>World prices of indium have fallen steadily in recent months. Nippon Mining last announced an indium price cut of 5,000 yen per kg on September 18, which followed price cuts in June and July.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
